<title>NETHERLANDS: SHARES IN ROYAL DUTCH FALL AFTER Q2 RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SHARES IN ROYAL DUTCH FALL AFTER Q2 RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in oil firm Royal Dutch Petroleum Co fell 4.20 guilders to 116.00 after the firm announced second quarter results and the stock remained volatile minutes after the announcement.</p>
<p>The group reported second quarter current cost income excluding special items of 1.140 billion sterling, which disappointed investors.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
